    "title": "Mobile Accessibility Task Force Meeting Resolutions",
    "text": "Minutes | Topics | Resolutions This page was last updated on 27 July 2026. For more recent meetings, see an alternative view of meeting minutes. 2017 23 February: Mobile Accessibility Task Force Teleconference touchscreen - have no additional techniques for 3.3.2, just add an example to the understanding documents, write the example that Patrick just did on the fly for G 131 2016 17 November: Mobile Accessibility Task Force Teleconference M11 - Accept changed language for success criteria, submit to working group with a note to email thread about SC 3.3.2 and 1.3.1 for working group evaluation M9 - submit M9 as modified M 16 - submit M16 as modified 27 October: Mobile Accessibility Task Force Teleconference M13 Orientation - this is been reviewed by task force and is now ready for working group review focus trap - drop M7 No Focus Trap for 2.1 20 October: Mobile Accessibility Task Force Teleconference M6 - Patrick to make final edits and ready for working group 29 September: Mobile Accessibility Task Force Teleconference will accept M15 Programmatic Notifications and submit to working group 8 September: Mobile Accessibility Task Force Teleconference Accidental Activation (finalize) - https://www.w3.org/WAI/GL/mobile-a11y-tf/wiki/Proposed_revision_of_2.5.3 - remove first SC, beef up second and third SC Accidental Activation (finalize) - https://www.w3.org/WAI/GL/mobile-a11y-tf/wiki/Proposed_revision_of_2.5.3 - remove first SC, make further editorial changes to 2nd/3rd SC, send 3rd to COGA for sync 1 September: Mobile Accessibility Task Force Teleconference target size is 48 and 24 px SC Target Size is accepted 18 August: Mobile Accessibility Task Force Teleconference SC Pointer with Assistive Technology - https://www.w3.org/WAI/GL/mobile-a11y-tf/wiki/Proposed_SC_Pointer_with_Assistive_Technology#SC_Shortname - https://www.w3.org/WAI/GL/mobile-a11y-tf/wiki/Proposed_SC_Pointer_with_Assistive_Technology#Benefits ready for WCAG 23 June: Mobile Accessibility Task Force Teleconference feedback from WCAG working group - add pointer definition to glossary and reference this definition where we generally mean pointing device 9 June: Mobile Accessibility Task Force Teleconference Finish 2.6.1 https://www.w3.org/WAI/GL/mobile-a11y-tf/wiki/Guideline_2.6:_Make_it_easier_to_use_the_physical_features_of_the_phone. - further discussion needed to write clear definition of pressure-sensitive input, to come up with use cases (easy and hard ones). see survey that will come on mailing list 2 June: Mobile Accessibility Task Force Teleconference remove force touch and touch from definition of device manipulation 21 April: Mobile Accessibility Task Force Teleconference review changes to Touch and Pointer - Accept the proposal as amended above (in wiki) for submission to WCAG WG. 3 March: Mobile Accessibility Task Force Teleconference 2.5.2 proposed Understanding text https://w3c.github.io/Mobile-A11y-Extension/#swipe-trap - revised Understanding text and to the Success Criteria of 2.5.2 No Swipe Trap to No Touch Trap 18 February: Mobile Accessibility Task Force Teleconference Finish 2.5.3 - https://w3c.github.io/Mobile-A11y-Extension/#touch-and-pointer - accept Intent for 2.5.2 Finish 2.5.3 - https://w3c.github.io/Mobile-A11y-Extension/#touch-and-pointer - accept Understanding for 2.5.2 11 February: Mobile Accessibility Task Force Teleconference Revisions to 2.5.3 Failure from Jonathan https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-mobile-a11y-tf/2016Feb/0008.html - Accept updates to the FM001 Failure of 2.5.3",
