    "title": "Maturity Model Task Force Meeting Resolutions",
    "text": "Minutes | Topics | Resolutions This page was last updated on 27 July 2026. For more recent meetings, see an alternative view of meeting minutes. 2025 15 October: Maturity Model Task Force Publication update - Return the referenced Excel to its previous location in the document Publication update - The APA Maturity Model Task Force has completed drafting its Accessibility Maturity Model (AMM) and requests that APA publish the draft currently at https://w3c.github.io/maturity-model/ as a Working Group Note. 13 August: Maturity Model Task Force W3C Accessibility Maturity Model Publication Update - Maturity Model group is ready for wide review of the editors draft prior to note status 26 February: Maturity Model Task Force Task Force Recharter Review - Recharter task force description to be option 2 19 February: Maturity Model Task Force Github Issue ##226 Add an explanatory section on dimension goals and metrics - The decision has been made to add an explanatory section on dimension goals and metrics at the beginning of Appendix, right before 4.1, according to Jeff's suggestion. Section 4.1 then becomes 4.2. 15 January: (MEETING TITLE) Publication Preparation - The approaches identified in this note are intended to influence organizational programs and advance accessibility focus from making digital assets and services accessible to creating an environment in which organizational maturity, specific to digital accessibility, may be measured and evaluated over time. This evolution towards Publication Preparation - The approaches identified in this note are intended to influence organizational programs and advance accessibility focus from making digital assets and services accessible to creating an environment in which organizational maturity, specific to digital accessibility, may be measured and evaluated over time. This evolution towards 2024 4 December: Maturity Model Task Force Github Issue #233 2.4 Assessment Template Needs Correcting - new wording to 2.4 is: The Maturity Model assessment template is a detailed prototype designed to track the accessibility maturity evaluation process outlined in this publication. Currently, it is available in Excel format. The future version is expected to be in HTML and may also be offered in other accessible, downloadable formats. Github Issue #234 2.4.1 Maturity Model Excel Spreadsheet Should be Deleted - will delete 2.4.1 Github Issue #232 Dimension Evaluation Instructions Are Problematic - change the wording to match the suggested text. 28 August: Maturity Model Task Force Github Issue GitHub Issue #155 Section 3.4: maturity also depends on how effective the ICT development processes are in producing accessible ICT. - Update - language approved GitHub Issue #129 Conflict in position Training Knowledge and Skills Vs. DLC - closing issue with proposed response GitHub Issue #52 Section 2 (and elsewhere, if necessary): broaden the range of standards relevant to the maturity model. - closing issue with proposed response 21 August: Maturity Model GitHub Issue ##130 Where to place &quot;internal support&quot; for MSE or dedicated A11Y Team? - Thank you, for your comment. We have taken it into consideration, along with other feedback from the public, and significantly revised the document. We believe that we have addressed your concern. If it still persists, please open a new issue, and provide any supporting documentation, you would like 24 July: Maturity Model Github Issue #143 communities of practice. Question, communities we serve? - Definition of Communities of Practice will be added as stated above 29 May: Maturity Model Task Force Github Issues 43, 78, 85, 102, 103, 104 (Usability doc feedback) â Look at Procurement Dimension - Maturity model task force APA request updated with current status 15 May: Maturity Model Github Issue #107 Definition of &quot;Full maturity&quot; needs to be adjusted, as there is no need to optimize anymore by then - Close issue 107 with comment: A maturity Model is a continuum, there is no end point. The Task Force has decided to keep the term optimize, as it suggests an ongoing effort without an end point. 24 January: MAgenda+ New Business Github Issue #89 ICT Development Lifecycle ratings outcomes aren't stated like the outcomes are in Silver - The Maturity Model is technology and standard agnostic. See section 2.3. If you have specific edits to suggest please provide a PR. 2023 6 December: Maturity Model Teleconference Working Draft EOY update - participants here approve a working draft update publication once the title has been updated. 15 November: Maturity Model Shall we meed Wednesday 22 November? - This TF will NOT meet on Wednesday 22 November. Our next telecon will be Wednesday 29 November End of Year Breaks - Maturity TF will meet through Wednesday 20 December, and resume on Wednesday 10 January. We will NOT meet on Wednesday 20 or Wednesday 27 December GitHub Issue #153 The effectiveness of knowledge/skill acquisition should be measured - We're closing 153 because Integrate and Optimize Outcome Stages include metrics and evaluation of performance 9 August: (MEETING TITLE) Discuss Publication Update - Have one file name for the maturity model exell document instead of each having its own date. 14 June: Msturity Model Stakeholder Spreadsheet - TO publish stakeholders document as an appendix, with an editor's note 8 February: Maturity Model Task Force Proposed Changes to clarify extensibility of the Maturity Model (see attached word doc) - We approve Sheri's suggested edits as caputred in https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-maturity/2023Feb/0010.html relating to equity and to extensibility for multiple business units in an organization/company, etc. 25 January: Maturity Model Intersection of Equity SubGroup and Maturity Model - AMM decides to remain focused on accessibility and extensibility 18 January: Maturity Model Subgroup Discussion on Sheris mail Maturity model homework - Drop #7 https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-rqtf/2023Jan/0015.html Discussion on Sheris mail Maturity model homework - Change wording in #5 to say establish and maintain https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-rqtf/2023Jan/0015.html 2022 10 August: (MEETING TITLE) Discuss FPWD Status - Move forward with messaging 3 August: Maturity Model RQTF Meeting Debrief - The Maturity Model Subgroup thanks RQTF for requesting a Call for Consensus from APA on a First Public Working Draft (FPWD) publication of our draft Maturity Model note-track document at https://w3c.github.io/maturity-model/index.html. An Excel spreadsheet that will assist users in implementing the Maturity Model will be attached to the CFC for review. 20 July: Maturity Model Meeting minutes - Have the entire spreadsheet downloadable at the top, and each dimension will refer to it's specific tab and the link will be before the table",
    "tags": "",
    "url": "/WAI/about/groups/task-forces/maturity-model/minutes/resolutions/"
