    "title": "Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Meeting Resolutions",
    "text": "Minutes | Topics | Resolutions This page was last updated on 27 July 2026. For more recent meetings, see an alternative view of meeting minutes. 2024 18 March: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference Meeting minutes - we follow the style guide at https://www.w3.org/Guide/manual-of-style/#ref-section , but we also let people refrence a row number in our database (clarify which database) which has the refrence. 2023 6 November: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference Meeting minutes - is the reserch plan V1 ready 31 July: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference issues . see https://github.com/w3c/coga/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+ - issue-1 WCAG processes reviewed by Rachael. issues . see https://github.com/w3c/coga/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+ - issue-2 Two discussion items in Github bugs review with new commentary (#305, 302) 2 March: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference Meeting minutes - Approve the outcomes as drafted in the Clear Language Working Draft 2022 12 July: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference determine what to focus on for this 1/2 hour - when writing pattern, method or objective names, bring the names back to the group for review and consensus before starting any detailed work 26 May: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference Check attendance plans for June 2 - we will hold our meeting next week as we have enough attendence 19 May: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference ICCHP https://www.icchp-aaate.org/ - FTF at icchp on july 12th - will be hybrid. 2021 11 November: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference Respond to open Internationalization issues - we will post this and clean up the issue queue. 9 September: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference Meta data and ISO response &lt;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TDPA3R1Y4hVn4Eq9NlRTZ_hg4cpd_8ZtpWoFiVuF_lk/edit&gt; - Share this document with ISO 1 April: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference publication updates - go with #4 in order to not have an objection 25 February: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference Actions &lt;https://www.w3.org/WAI/GL/task-forces/coga/wiki/PlanningPage#Timelines_and_actions&gt; - Make small changes including fixing easy and leave section 5.4 in but add framing language Actions &lt;https://www.w3.org/WAI/GL/task-forces/coga/wiki/PlanningPage#Timelines_and_actions&gt; - Make small changes including fixing easy and leave section 5.4 in but add framing language CFC for icons as in https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-cognitive-a11y-tf/2021Feb/0121.html - Use new icon of stickies in thought bubble 11 February: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference Inclusive language - Move forward with identity-first language throughout Content Usable for autistic people, knowing we will have an explanatory paragraph 28 January: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference actions: https://www.w3.org/WAI/GL/task-forces/coga/wiki/PlanningPage#Timelines_and_ - Use Autistic with clarification language 25 January: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference Framing language - add Following this guidance to the introduction and revised wording discussed here. Friendly vs Usable - \"Making websites and applications usable by people with cognitive impairments affects every part of design and development.\" Change friendly to usable everywhere in the document and change to active voice. Sentence vs. List Structure - Make it a list. Framing language - Unbold the word essential âThe Objectives and Patterns build on the..â - leave current language âSome design patterns create barriers for people with disabilitiesâ - Some common designs create barriers for people with disabilities. judy's point - Judy, Rachael, LIsa, John, and Shawn to rework the paragraph to be more forward facing. 7 January: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference aprove or disscuss: merging apendisis with new title https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-cognitive-a11y-tf/2021Jan/0012.html - Merge appendices B and D 2020 19 November: SV_MEETING_TITLE Status updates and Actions https://www.w3.org/WAI/GL/task-forces/coga/wiki/PlanningPage#Timelines_and_actions - Publish the glossary with an unaltered version of content usable for a review of the glossary (after CFC on COGA lis) Email with changes from Lisa's editorial pass - Rewrite the examples by adding a short introductory sentence that meets the verbal pattern. Review all examples to see if any obvious ones are missing. Email with changes from Lisa's editorial pass - Rewrite the examples by adding a short introductory sentence that meets the verbal pattern. Review all examples to see if any obvious ones are missing. 29 October: SV_MEETING_TITLE Review image language - Approve language 15 October: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference actions: https://www.w3.org/WAI/GL/task-forces/coga/wiki/PlanningPage - Accept adding a bullet to the decision policy agreement section on Ideally based on research-supported recommendations 24 September: COGA process review https://www.w3.org/WAI/GL/task-forces/coga/wiki/Process_proposal - Move the decision on the decision policy to a list (it is a large item) 17 September: Cognitive and Learning Disabilities Accessibility Task Force Teleconference Status updates and Actions &lt;https://www.w3.org/WAI/GL/task-forces/coga/wiki/PlanningPage#Timelines_and_actions&gt; - Revised template approved. 30 July: COGA 30 July 2020 Proposed Issue Response https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fc7TI8V6dNgFrD6wzGR8CjbbtO7Az0U-zYylrRSy8QQ/edit - Cleanup and email out for final review 9 July: COGA Taskforce 9 July 2020 Glossary - ADD disclaimer language to beginning of glossary. Glossary - Consistent approach to language with alternatives in () beside term in definition. Glossary - Use person first pending confirmation by wider group by email list 25 June: SV_MEETING_TITLE July 2nd Meeting - Should we hold it? - Hold it unless we receive more regrets next week Critical terms for the glossary - Defintion of AD(H)D approved 7 May: COGA Taskforce 7 May 2020 How to go forward (Process)? - AG prioritizes and consolidates comments. Then COGA suggests fixes. 23 April: COGA taskforce 23 April 2020 glossary terms - Move forward with working group review 16 April: Cognitive Accessibility Task Force Teleconference wcag review of indicators - Coga wants to see visual indicators added and will work on a proposal for Tuesday 20 February: coga tf meeting Leave technical details in patterns but renamed \"Alternative versions\" and \"The following are alternative versions with some suggested test techniques.\" 2019 21 November: Cognitive Accessibility Task Force Teleconference Planning and Actions https://www.w3.org/WAI/GL/task-forces/coga/wiki/PlanningPage - cancel next week 2016 12 December: Cognitive Accessibility Task Force Teleconference Tables of user needs https://rawgit.com/w3c/coga/master/gap-analysis/table.html - Publish new tables, not old ones. 4 January: SV_MEETING_TITLE we should have a ftf in lisbon lisa to set up poll for next ftf",
