    "title": "Spoken Presentation Task Force Meeting Resolutions",
    "text": "Minutes | Topics | Resolutions This page was last updated on 27 July 2026. For more recent meetings, see an alternative view of meeting minutes. 2025 14 July: (MEETING TITLE) Administrivia - Deprecate the Gap Analysis and Use Cases document at &lt;https://www.w3.org/TR/pronunciation-gap-analysis-and-use-cases/&gt;, and refer instead to the separate Use Cases (at &lt;https://www.w3.org/TR/pronunciation-use-cases/&gt;), and Gap Analysis (at &lt;https://www.w3.org/TR/pronunciation-gap-analysis/&gt;), documents. Administrivia - Deprecate the User Scenarios document at &lt;https://www.w3.org/TR/pronunciation-user-scenarios/&gt;, and refer instead to the Use Cases document (at &lt;https://www.w3.org/TR/pronunciation-use-cases/&gt;). 2021 7 April: Spoken Pronunciation Task Force Teleconference Meeting minutes - The Spoken Presentation Task Force requests APA issue a Call for Consensus to publish https://w3c.github.io/pronunciation/technical-approach/ as a FPWD. 2019 14 August: Pronunciation Task Force Teleconference Timeline for Gap Analysis Document https://w3c.github.io/pronunciation/gap-analysis/ - Pronunciation TF requests that APA Call for Consensus to publish our Gap Analysis as a First Public Working Draft, with the understanding that we will complete all content currently present which doesn't completely express our concept. Timeline for User Scenarios Document https://w3c.github.io/pronunciation/user-scenarios/ - Pronunciation TF requests that APA Call for Consensus to publish our User Scenarios as a First Public Working Draft, with the understanding that we will complete all content currently present which doesn't completely express our concept.",
