    "title": "Accessible Platform Architectures Working Group Meeting Resolutions",
    "text": "Minutes | Topics | Resolutions This page was last updated on 27 July 2026. For more recent meetings, see an alternative view of meeting minutes. 2025 21 May: APA Weekly Teleconference Charter - Proceed with current Charter draft with minimal &quot;Deliverables&quot; edits 30 April: APA Weekly Teleconference Re-chartering - Best Practices for Author-Controlled Pronunciation 2024 8 May: APA Weekly Teleconference CSS View Transitions w3c/a11y-review#192 - APA would like to see view transitions disablable. 2023 1 November: APA Weekly Teleconference Privacy Working Group - APA supports charter for Privacy Group as drafted. Web Application Security WG - APA supports charter for Web Application Security WG as drafted. 27 September: APA Teleconference Epub Note Special Request https://w3c.github.io/epub-specs/epub33/a11y-exemption/ - APA approves and supports the Epub Note on accessibility metadata and does not object to the Note's publication. 1 February: Accessible Platform Architectures (APA) Weekly Teleconference APA Rechartering: Ready for CfC? https://github.com/w3c/apa/blob/charter-2023/charter.html - APA avers we are ready for a Call for Consensus on our draft proposed Charter at https://github.com/w3c/apa/blob/charter-2023/charter.html 4 January: APA Teleconference Actions Checkin (Specs) https://www.w3.org/WAI/APA/track/actions/open - APA approves the three specifications in the EPUB 3.3 family. 2022 7 December: APA Weekly Teleconference Advancing Adapt Symbols to CR - APA confirms support for advancing Adapt Symbol Module to CR based on our previous consensus which included symbols logged at https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-apa-admin/2022Aug/0058.html 24 August: Accessible Platform Architectures Working Group Teleconference APA Review of Draft AGWG Charter https://raw.githack.com/w3c/wcag/charter-2022/charter.html - Current draft charter on github is not meaningful path forward APA Review of Draft AGWG Charter https://raw.githack.com/w3c/wcag/charter-2022/charter.html - APA confirms it considers both WCAG 2.2 and WCAG 3 important for accessibility and wishes to say each of them proceed unimpeded. 10 August: Accessible Platform Architectures Working Group Teleconference CSS Color Level 5 review - https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-apa/2022Aug/0002.html - APA will run a CfC to make Matthew_Atkinson's CSS comments (with proposed revisions) an APA comment 2016 7 September: Accessible Platform Architectures Working Group Teleconference Actions Checkin (Specs) https://www.w3.org/WAI/APA/track/products/8 - no comments to file for action 2085 4 August: Accessible Platform Architectures Working Group Teleconference API &amp; Payments Architecture Review - We will write some accessibility text to recommend be included in each of the Web Payments API specifications, and use this as the basis of a CFC for APA WG. 27 July: Accessible Platform Architectures Working Group Teleconference Actions Checkin (Specs) https://www.w3.org/WAI/APA/track/products/8 - Take Janina's draft email for action 2067 Actions Checkin (Specs) https://www.w3.org/WAI/APA/track/products/8 - Take Janina's draft email to CfC for action 2067 22 June: Accessible Platform Architectures Working Group Teleconference UI Events review - Cynthia to send feedback on UI Events to CSS working group 15 June: Accessible Platform Architectures Working Group Teleconference COGA FPWD Update -- Lisa, Michael - Publish the two documents referenced by Lisa above as FPWD. 1 June: Accessible Platform Architectures Working Group Teleconference RQTF Formation https://www.w3.org/WAI/APA/task-forces/research-questions/work-statement - Issue CfC RQTF Work Statement 27 January: Accessible Platform Architectures Working Group Teleconference Decision Policy -- Ready for CfC? http://www.w3.org/WAI/APA/decision-policy - meeting agrees to take Draft Decision Policy to CfC",
