    "title": "Examples of Visible",
    "text": "These are examples of the visible definition. The examples presented here are non-normative and not testable. They serve to illustrate some common pitfalls about the definition and to help implementers of ACT rules understand it. Default visibility This span element is visible (by default, elements are visible). &lt;span&gt;Now you can see me!&lt;/span&gt; Hidden with CSS visibility This span element is not visible because of the CSS visibility property. &lt;span style=\"visibility: hidden\"&gt;I'm the invisible man&lt;/span&gt; Hidden with CSS display This span element is not visible because of the CSS display property. &lt;span style=\"display: none\"&gt;I'm the invisible man&lt;/span&gt; Hidden with CSS position These span elements are not visible because they are positioned off-screen. Note that depending on device size and actual position of the span elements, they might be visible on some larger device or long pages. &lt;span style=\"position: absolute; top: -9999px; left: -9999px;\"&gt;Incredible how you can&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=\"position: absolute; top: -9999px\"&gt;See right through me&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=\"position: absolute; left: -9999px;\"&gt;When you hear a sound&lt;/span&gt; Hidden due to a lack of content This span element is not visible because it contains only whitespace and line breaks. &lt;span&gt; &lt;br /&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt; This span element is not visible because its text content has size 0. &lt;span style=\"font-size: 0px\"&gt;That you just can't place&lt;/span&gt; Hidden due to matching colors This span element is not visible because it has the exact same color as its background. &lt;span style=\"color: #00F; background: #00F;\"&gt;Feel something move&lt;/span&gt; Hidden due to transparency This span element is not visible because it has no opacity. &lt;span style=\"opacity: 0\"&gt;That you just can't trace&lt;/span&gt; This span element is not visible because it’s text is fully transparent. &lt;span style=\"color: transparent\"&gt;When something sits&lt;/span&gt; Hidden due to clipping This span element is not visible because it’s size is reduced to zero, and any overflow is hidden. &lt;span style=\"height: 0px; width: 0px; overflow: hidden\"&gt;On the end of your bed&lt;/span&gt; This span element is not visible because its content is fully indented out of it, and any overflow is hidden. &lt;span style=\"text-indent: -200%; overflow: hidden\"&gt;Don't turn around&lt;/span&gt; This span element is not visible because it is clipped to zero size. &lt;span style=\"clip-path: inset(50%)\"&gt;When you hear me tread&lt;/span&gt; Hidden due to transformation This div element is not visible because it is scaled to 0%. &lt;div style=\"transform: scale(0%)\"&gt;I'm the invisible man&lt;/div&gt; This div element is not visible because it is translated out of screen. &lt;div style=\"transform: translate(-100%)\"&gt;I'm the invisible man&lt;/div&gt; Glossary Visible Content perceivable through sight. Content is considered visible if making it fully transparent would result in a difference in the pixels rendered for any part of the document that is currently within the viewport or can be brought into the viewport via scrolling.",
    "tags": "",
    "url": "/WAI/standards-guidelines/act/rules/terms/visible/examples/"
